nd answer every finding explicitly.\n3|P1 (all four must be fixed; each needs a committed test that fails on the current code):\n4|- P1-1 event authority (§5.2, §2.4): `run.go emitParked` authors `session.parked` under `observation.Winner`'s lease even when the winner is REMOTE, manufacturing a sequence collision on a lease this host does not hold (reviewer probes 1, 1b, 2, 9, 15). Author parked evidence only under a lease the local host actually holds — or through a host-local, non-chain record if the pinned text gives no local lease — gate every `Emit` through the landed `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` (today there are zero callers of AuthorizeMutation/AuthorizeInput anywhere, while doc.go:29 claims AuthorizeInput is composed), and refuse to author a lifecycle event that the §5.7 transition table cannot fold from the derived state (`sessstate.Reduce` currently refuses the wrapper's own fixture chain with `invalid_state_transition`). Probe 15's blast radius must close too: an event appended under a losing lease must not become the effective profile source. The pre-existing tail-only acceptance in `sessrepo.checkAppend` is NOT yours to fix (a separate board item carries it) — but this leaf must not build a new writer that depends on it.\n5|- P1-2 realm authorization (§4.2, §13.11, §4.D): `decide.go checkRealm` returns nil on the bare boolean `input.Realm.AttestedServer`, so a background caller launches with a stale tmux server generation or with no realm evidence at all (probe 3), and `checkSmoke` binds only provider/version/platform/arch while `Target.TmuxServerGeneration`/`MacOSVersion` are pure refusal decoration. Require the admitted §4.D `credential_capable_execution_realm` Capability Evidence row (terminal_binding_id, provider_id/build, sentinel_result, provider_auth_smoke_result, backend_generation_digest, os_version, expires_at, signature) bound to the exact host binding, the probed provider build and the CURRENT generation, admitted through the landed `terminalbackend` reconcile path; drop the bare boolean as an authorizing input; make expiry/logout/reboot invalidation real. Then make the README sentence \"no cached sentinel or managername observation can authorize resume\" true as worded, and replace the field-NAME reflection census with a test that proves a cached observation cannot authorize.\n6|- P1-3 bootstrap window (§4.1, §13.1, §4.C restore row): the receipt is keyed by `session_id` alone and any different operation is refused forever, so after the window closes the whole after-restore sequence is unreachable on a host that once created the session (probe 5). Model the window: key the receipt per operation (`session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id`) or supersede it, close the window at the first checkpoint using the winner's own `HasCheckpoint`/epoch already present in `Observation`, keep \"changed operation INSIDE the window = idempotency_mismatch\", and allow `create` from `stopped`. The reviewer's mutant RM4 (idempotency arm dropped for restore mode) survived the whole suite twice — add the restore-mode idempotency tests that kill it and say so with the raw log.\n7|- P1-4 checkpoint admission (§13.11 step 5): `admitCheckpoint` only checks digest self-consistency against a caller-supplied id, so an older checkpoint (probe 6) and a checkpoint captured for a DIFFERENT session (probe 6b) both authorize a launch. Admit exactly the winning lease's checkpoint (`Winner.Checkpoint`) and bind the checkpoint's own `session_id` through the landed `sessckpt` admission/head-binding path.\n8|P2 (same rework): P2-1 derive the effective profile on resume from the validated checkpoint's event-head closure (`sessprofile.DeriveForHeads`), not the session head (probe 8), and re-pin the PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME row with a test that actually runs in resume mode with a checkpoint; P2-2 bind the materialization journal to the lease checkpoint (`SourceCheckpointID` vs `Winner.Checkpoint`), not `Phase == committed` alone (probe 7); P2-3 make `Interactive` a `Decide` input and evaluate the §4.C create-row conditional `headless_creation` for a non-interactive create (probe 4); P2-4 fix the after-restore step-5 label — a remote owner outside an interactive terminal is `parked`, not `takeover_offer` — and correct the committed test and TRACEABILITY row that pin it wrong; P2-5 kill the two remaining survived reviewer mutants with committed tests: RM1 (a swallowed `ObserveOwnership` error must stay an error, \"unknown is never absence\" must hold for the lease path, not only the pane store) and RM2 (the after-restore precedence must pin the order of the materialization and authorize arms, not just their presence).\n9|P3: sweep the `binding-*.tmp` staging file left by a pre-commit crash; fix the TRACEABILITY mutant table (the `N-discovery` row is listed twice: 26 rows shown for a 25-row harness); fix the `doc.go:29` claim about `AuthorizeInput`; and soften or justify the \"nothing re-implemented\" claim where `ParkedPayload`/`checkEvidenceIDs` duplicate closed-shape predicates `canonicaljson` already enforces. The reviewer's P3-3 (landed `fencing.Authorize` expiry-before-direction ordering and `sessrepo.checkAppend` stale-lease tail acceptance) is NOT yours — the orchestrator files those as their own board items; do not change those packages.\n10|Coverage: the producer claim was 41 of 41 AC rows driven; the reviewer's honest ratio for revision 1 is 35 of 41. Re-derive the ratio yourself after the fixes, list each of the six previously unfaithful rows with the new test that drives it, and do not restate a number you did not measure.\n11|Procedure: the managed Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree (branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe) still holds your uncommitted candidate on base 7efe385; origin/main has since moved to 888ae3d (one commit, `task-board.config.json` only: command 5 became `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`). FIRST run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-