{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c0-ed80-7083-a928-581e7c42de76"},"sequence":68,"recorded_at":1780531400000131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"59f95e0c-e6e0-4829-ade8-6c5cffb39d86","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"59f95e0c-e6e0-4829-ade8-6c5cffb39d86","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"59f95e0c-e6e0-4829-ade8-6c5cffb39d86"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0c1191d7430ab2ce3d8285116c6","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-1geqhj/TASK-260830-1geqhj_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-1geqhj (implement-ax-pane-enforcement-wrapper), first leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe (ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding, EPIC M1; siblings 2056mm and kkh1an follow). Implement, as production code over the landed owners, the validation core of the `ax pane SESSION_ID` wrapper that every managed pane runs (pinned Section 4.C wrapper rule: validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize known lease records when possible, compare the local fencing token before launching a provider, park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous or unverified; the after-restore sequence 1-5: read the latest locally known lease, attempt a bounded mesh lease refresh, resume locally only with the winning lease AND a valid required materialization, offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session interactively, otherwise enter parked without launching the provider; terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start idempotent on (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) with the pair durably bound before child creation, identical retry reattaching to the one recorded wrapper/child, changed operation in the bootstrap window = idempotency_mismatch, status plus the binding proving absence or identifying the one child after a lost result; never persist or replicate a PID; no credential-dependent tmux server creation from a background caller — capability_unavailable with typed realm/readiness details, never direct server creation; cached sentinel/managername never authorizes resume), Section 4.B (Terminal Backend Manifest/Probe identity through the landed internal/terminalbackend registry and contract), Section 4.D (closed capabilities and evidence: only the exact admitted capability rows authorize an action; no capability map invented), Section 5.2 Terminal Events (the events the wrapper authors: session.parked with its reason vocabulary, terminal binding/evidence events as the schema defines them — author them through the landed sessrepo append path under the current lease), Section 7.A (Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding descriptor: terminal_binding_id, terminal_instance_id UUIDv7 never a PID/handle, backend id/version/protocol/generation, interactive, columns/rows — the wrapper supplies it and the provider must reject a mismatched binding; the LeaseToken is passed separately) and Section 13.1 Direct-session launch steps 3-4 (create the durable terminal entry with the bootstrap operation ID, then provider launch with its validated argv/env plan). The wrapper's checks must be composed from the landed gates rather than re-implemented: owner epoch/fencing through internal/fencing (AuthorizeActivation/Input/Restore, the sealed LeaseToken projection, park vocabulary), materialization validity through internal/matjournal + internal/sessckpt admission, profile through internal/sessprofile (effective persisted profile + Section 7.7 mapping refusals, profile_mapping_unavailable), provider identity through internal/provhost (CreateIdentity/Verify*, resume tuple gate, resumesmoke evidence as a precondition input), resume authorization through the fencing gates plus the checkpoint admission. Deliver a library entry (for example internal/axpane) with a pure decision core (inputs: config, session record + chain, local lease view, materialization/journal state, profile, provider identity, terminal backend probe, realm readiness; output: exactly one of launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked(reason)|refused(class)) plus the durable bootstrap binding (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) under the landed no-replace + fsync discipline with crash hooks and a real-kill test; no `ax` CLI, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider process — those are modeled callers and later leaves (state the bound). Tests: every decision outcome driven with positives and the full refusal/park table (lower/losing epoch, foreign session, expired grant, absent/ambiguous/remote ownership, invalid materialization, unmapped profile, unresolved provider identity or realm, backend probe mismatch, background caller without an attested server, changed bootstrap operation in-window, lost-result reattach), the after-restore sequence as a scenario table, idempotency of the bootstrap binding, crash at the binding seam, narrowing mutants per gate composition (each composition check dropped or reordered must be caught), and a conformance matrix over 4.B/4.C/4.D/5.2/7.A/13.1 clauses.\n2|COMMON CONTRACT (first leaf of a Story on trunk 7efe385 or later). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named below; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260916-3uqbwq) is landing during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) — never fork a second model; extend or adopt. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this first leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and re-pin once the v0.7.0 registry is on trunk; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix instead. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED; never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-1geqhj` (LOGBOOK append conflicts are resolved with --replay-resolutions: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add {\"checkpoint_oid\": <REBASE_HEAD original checkpoint>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>} keeping every entry newest-first), then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that appears in your git status and restore trunk content by hand (README/LOGBOOK purely additive; task-board.config.json == HEAD); before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured 26-command validation suite once before handoff (command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted … -check`); hand off no later than 3.5 hours in — if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-1geqhj_results.md, TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-1geqhj_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-1geqhj --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
