{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c54f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c0-ed80-7083-a928-581e7c42de76"},"sequence":258,"recorded_at":1780531400000511,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"59f95e0c-e6e0-4829-ade8-6c5cffb39d86","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"59f95e0c-e6e0-4829-ade8-6c5cffb39d86","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"59f95e0c-e6e0-4829-ade8-6c5cffb39d86"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0c1-a3dd-70c0-960f-4b7c3dd47961"},"task_id":"01a0b0c1-a3dd-70c0-960f-4b7c3dd47961","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0c1-a3dd-70c0-960f-4b7c3dd47961","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj — independent review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-1geqhj-1 revision 1\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED (routed `to-dev`).** Four P1 classes, five P2, three P3.\n4|\n5|Reviewer: RUN-260917-3934e0 (claude-opus-5 max). Reviewed bytes: base\n6|`7efe3854a5a14545f9fa2b7697accb1883249f1f`, candidate tree\n7|`bb8dbdebcd5102a772960d8399661a2b2dcae0c1` (recomputed from the live worktree\n8|with an untracked-aware temporary index: equal), patch sha256\n9|`472870c8b6c2f69e54a8de0901e0ccf127f3f4aee4d85bbe070d45339043c3b8` (equal to the CR record). All probes ran in an isolated\n10|`git archive` copy under `.temp/TASK-260830-1geqhj/review/`; the live Story\n11|worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched. Every instrument, raw\n12|log and subprocess exit is in `TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`\n13|(paths below are relative to that archive).\n14|\n15|## What holds (verified myself)\n16|\n17|| Check | Result | Evidence |\n18|| --- | --- | --- |\n19|| gofmt / go vet / go build on the exact tree | exit 0 / 0 / 0 | `logs/01-03`, `logs/70-tree-exact-checks.log` |\n20|| GOOS=linux, GOOS=windows builds | exit 0 / 0 | `logs/70` |\n21|| tracecheck (registry untouched) | exit 0, contracts=63 sections=36 | `logs/70` |\n22|| `cataloggen -adopted … -check` | exit 0 | `logs/70` |\n23|| `go test ./internal/axpane -count=1 -v` | exit 0, 119 PASS lines | `logs/05-*` |\n24|| axpane+fencing+sessprofile+matjournal+sessckpt+provhost | all ok, exit 0 | `logs/71-six-packages.log` |\n25|| Shipped mutant harness, isolated copy, two full passes | 25/25 match both passes (24 KILLED ×2, control SURVIVED ×2); blobs restored (OIDs equal to candidate tree) | `logs/40`, `logs/41`, `logs/42-43` |\n26|| Real-kill after commit (`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`) ×2 | PASS ×2 | `logs/60` |\n27|| My real SIGKILL before commit (AfterStage) | restart proves absence (found=false, err=nil); retry installs exactly one `binding.json`; never a second child | `logs/10` probe C1 |\n28|| Identical retries with different child facts ×3 | same inode, same mtime, same bytes, session dir has 1 entry | `logs/10` probe C2 |\n29|| Receipt shape / PID | 7 closed members, no PID/handle/socket; `pid` appears only in comments | `logs/80-hygiene.log` |\n30|| Changed paths | exactly the 21 candidate paths; 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in tree; `internal/traceability` untouched | `logs/80` |\n31|| Capability outside the closed §4.D set (`teleport`) | refused `terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch` before Decide | probe 12 |\n32|| Descriptor generation ≠ host binding | refused `terminal_backend_stale_generation` | probe 13 |\n33|| Arm precedence (invalid config + changed op) | `invalid_config` wins | probe 11 |\n34|| Race gate (`internal/sessquery -race`) | **host-capacity artifact, not a regression**: my rerun exit 0 in 656 s (`-timeout 25m`) with load 13→27 and 11 other `go test` processes — *not* an idle host; import census 0/0 both directions; the candidate touches no sessquery byte; the only README/LOGBOOK reference in sessquery is `testdata/mutate.py`. The configured `go test ./... -race` without `-timeout` is a latent trunk flake for whoever owns CI, not this leaf. | `logs/30`, `logs/20-import-census.log` |\n35|\n36|## P1 — must fix before this leaf can be accepted\n37|\n38|### P1-1 §5.2 event authority: `session.parked` is authored under a lease the local host does not hold\n39|`run.go:245-282` (`emitParked`) always authors under `observation.Winner`\n40|(`LeaseEpoch: observation.Winner.Epoch`, `LeaseID: observation.Winner.LeaseID`)\n41|with `created_by_host_id = LocalHostID`. For every `remote_owner` park (both\n42|offers) and for unverified/ambiguous/failed-handoff parks whose winner is\n43|remote, that lease belongs to another host. §5.2: \"The winning owner MUST\n44|serialize state-changing events … two different events at one sequence under\n45|the winning lease … is `invalid_state_transition`; the session MUST park\".\n46|\n47|- Probe 1 (`TestReviewProbeRemoteOwnerParkedEventLease`): after a graceful\n48|  takeover to `fixtureRemoteHost` (lease B, epoch 2) `Run` → `takeover_offer`\n49|  and writes `session.parked` with `lease_id=B epoch=2 seq=1\n50|  created_by=<local host>`. The owner's own first event at (B, seq 1) is then\n51|  refused locally: `event lease sequence 1 repeats chained sequence through 1`\n52|  — the collision the spec forbids, manufactured by the parked host.\n53|- Probe 1b: `Verified=false` with a remote winner → `parked(restore_policy)`\n54|  authored under the remote-held lease B as well.\n55|- Probe 2 (`TestReviewProbeParkedEventFoldsInStateEngine`): the chain the\n56|  candidate's own fixtures produce (`session.created` → wrapper's\n57|  `session.parked`) is refused by the landed `sessstate.Reduce`:\n58|  `invalid_state_transition: event session.parked … moves \"creating\" to\n59|  \"parked\" without a Section 5.7 edge`. The wrapper never consults the\n60|  lifecycle state before authoring a lifecycle-changing event; only\n61|  materializing/stopped/failed may move to parked.\n62|- Probe 9 (`TestReviewProbeEmitUnderLosingLease`): `EmitParked` under the\n63|  superseded lease A (epoch 1) with the tail still at A is **accepted**\n64|  (`err=nil`); the landed repo only refuses once the tail has moved\n65|  (`ErrStaleLease`). `Emit` (`events.go:161-212`) never composes\n66|  `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` — grep: zero callers of `AuthorizeMutation`/\n67|  `AuthorizeInput` anywhere; `doc.go:29` nevertheless lists `AuthorizeInput`\n68|  as composed.\n69|- Probe 15 (`TestReviewProbeLosingLeaseProfileEventDrivesLaunch`) shows the\n70|  blast radius of the same hole: a `profile.changed` appended under losing\n71|  lease A after local successor A2 won is accepted by the chain and then\n72|  **drives the launch**: `profile=yolo source=<losing event>\n73|  mapping=\"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\"`. §2.4: \"Losing-lease\n74|  or ambiguous events MUST NOT change [the effective profile]\".\n75|\n76|Required: author parked evidence only under a lease the local host holds\n77|(or through the landed parked channel / a non-chain host-local record —\n78|the orchestrator/spec decides), gate every `Emit` through\n79|`fencing.AuthorizeMutation` (the landed \"event append\" entry), and refuse to\n80|author a lifecycle event the §5.7 table cannot fold from the derived state.\n81|The pre-existing tail-only acceptance in `sessrepo.checkAppend` is a landed\n82|property worth a separate board item; it is not this leaf's to fix, but this\n83|leaf must not build a new writer on it.\n84|\n85|### P1-2 §4.2 realm rule: an unbound boolean authorizes a background resume\n86|`decide.go:582-603` (`checkRealm`): `if input.Realm.AttestedServer { return\n87|nil }`. The only \"structural\" defence (`TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence`) is\n88|a reflection census of field *names*; it proves that no field is *called*\n89|cached-sentinel, not that a cached observation cannot authorize.\n90|\n91|- Probe 3 (`TestReviewProbeAttestedServerBooleanAuthorizes`): background\n92|  caller, `AttestedServer=true`, `Smoke.Required=true`, passing smoke record,\n93|  `Target.TmuxServerGeneration=\"generation-STALE-pre-reboot\"` (≠ the backend's\n94|  raw generation) → **launch**; admitted set\n95|  `[durable_disconnect headless_creation local_attach reboot_restoration]` —\n96|  no `credential_capable_execution_realm` row exists anywhere in the\n97|  universe, and with `Smoke.Required=false` the same boolean launches with no\n98|  realm evidence at all.\n99|- `checkSmoke` (`decide.go:537-556`) binds provider/version/platform/arch\n100|  only; the resumesmoke record carries no tmux-server generation, macOS\n101|  version or expiry. `Target.TmuxServerGeneration`/`MacOSVersion` are refusal\n102|  decoration, never compared to anything. §4.2: \"Evidence MUST bind the exact\n103|  tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version … Logout or\n104|  reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. A cached sentinel or prior\n105|  managername observation MUST NOT authorize resume.\" §13.11: background\n106|  restore \"MUST NOT … infer provider authentication from launchctl\n107|  managername or a cached sentinel.\"\n108|- The landed composition target exists and is unused: §4.D\n109|  `credential_capable_execution_realm` Capability Evidence (terminal_binding_id,\n110|  provider_id/build, sentinel_result, provider_auth_smoke_result,\n111|  backend_generation_digest, os_version, expires_at, signature) admitted by\n112|  `terminalbackend.Reconcile`; §4.C names it as the create/restore dependency\n113|  \"when provider credentials are required\". `terminalbackend.CheckOperation`'s\n114|  own doc assigns the conditional dependencies to \"the lifecycle owner\" —\n115|  this wrapper — and the wrapper never evaluates them.\n116|- README claim \"no cached sentinel or `managername` observation can authorize\n117|  resume\" is therefore unsupported as worded.\n118|\n119|Required: for a background caller / credential-requiring path require the\n120|admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to the exact host\n121|binding, probed provider build and current generation (the landed evidence\n122|object carries all of it); drop the bare boolean as an authorizing input.\n123|\n124|### P1-3 Bootstrap window not modeled: one binding per session, forever\n125|`binding.go:92-98,125-134` keys the receipt by `session_id` only and refuses\n126|*any* different operation (`existing.OperationID != operationID` →\n127|`idempotency_mismatch`), and `decide.go:321` mirrors it. §4.1: \"changing the\n128|operation for a session still in the bootstrap window is\n129|idempotency_mismatch\"; §13.1 closes the window at the first checkpoint; the\n130|§4.C `restore` row carries its own `bootstrap_operation_id` with key\n131|`session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id`; `create` is allowed from\n132|`stopped`.\n133|\n134|- Probe 5 (`TestReviewProbeSecondBootstrapOperationAfterWindow`): create\n135|  binds op1; a successor lease with the captured checkpoint closes the window;\n136|  `Run(ModeRestore, op2, committed materialization, admitted checkpoint)` →\n137|  **refused `idempotency_mismatch`** (\"changed inside the bootstrap window\").\n138|  On any host that once created the session, the entire after-restore\n139|  sequence is unreachable and no API can clear the receipt.\n140|- The winner's `HasCheckpoint`/epoch (already in `Observation`) is the\n141|  landed fact that defines the window; the store needs a per-operation key\n142|  (or supersession) plus the window predicate.\n143|- Reviewer mutant RM4 (idempotency arm dropped for restore mode) **survived\n144|  the whole suite twice**; witness under the mutant: restore + changed\n145|  operation → `reattach` to a child bound under *another* operation. No\n146|  restore-mode idempotency test exists.\n147|\n148|### P1-4 Checkpoint admission is unbound to session and lease\n149|`decide.go:496-508` (`admitCheckpoint`) = digest self-consistency +\n150|equality with a *caller-supplied* id; `gates.go:120` loads any digest from\n151|`sessckpt` with no session scoping.\n152|\n153|- Probe 6 (`TestReviewProbeCheckpointNotLeaseCheckpoint`): winning lease\n154|  checkpoint `sha256:c9c9…`, caller names the older `sha256:83ec…` → **launch**.\n155|  §13.11 step 5: \"validate the newest checkpoint\".\n156|- Probe 6b (`TestReviewProbeForeignCheckpointAdmitted`): a valid checkpoint\n157|  captured for session `…90ff` is admitted for resume of session `…90ab` →\n158|  **launch**. The checkpoint's own `session_id`/lease members are never read.\n159|\n160|Required: admit exactly the winning lease's checkpoint (`Winner.Checkpoint`)\n161|and bind its `session_id` (the landed `sessckpt.Admit`/head-binding path or\n162|the attested members) — \"resume authorization through the fencing gates plus\n163|the checkpoint admission\" currently has no admission.\n164|\n165|## P2 — fix in the same rework\n166|\n167|- **P2-1 Profile authority on resume uses the session head, not the\n168|  checkpoint closure.** `decide.go:378` calls `sessprofile.Derive` in every\n169|  mode; §13.10: \"For a validated checkpoint, derive the exact effective\n170|  profile/source from its event-head closure\"; the landed entry is\n171|  `DeriveForHeads`. Probe 8: resume from C1 (closure `[created]`) with a\n172|  head-only `profile.changed` E2 → launch carries `yolo/E2`. TRACEABILITY\n173|  claims the PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME direction; the test that \"pins\" it\n174|  (`TestDecideProfileSourcePinsEvent`) runs in launch mode without a\n175|  checkpoint.\n176|- **P2-2 Materialization \"valid\" = `Phase == committed` only**\n177|  (`decide.go:344`). Probe 7: a committed journal whose\n178|  `source_checkpoint_id` is one generation behind the lease checkpoint →\n179|  launch. Bind the journal to the lease checkpoint (the journal carries\n180|  `SourceCheckpointID`; the winner carries `Checkpoint`).\n181|- **P2-3 `headless_creation` conditional never evaluated.** `Interactive` is\n182|  not a `Decide` input; probe 4: non-interactive create with probed\n183|  `headless_creation=false` (durable_disconnect still confers create) →\n184|  launch. §4.C create row: \"`headless_creation` when non-interactive\".\n185|- **P2-4 Step-5 label.** Probe 14 / producer row `takeover_offer_noninteractive`:\n186|  a remote owner outside an interactive terminal yields `takeover_offer`;\n187|  §4.2 step 5: \"enter parked without launching the provider in all other\n188|  cases\". Durable effect is the same parked event, so this is a label, but\n189|  it is pinned wrong by a committed test and copied into TRACEABILITY.\n190|- **P2-5 Survived reviewer mutants (full suite as killer, 2/2 runs, deltas\n191|  witnessed under each mutant, `logs/50-53`):**\n192|  - RM1 — `ObserveOwnership` error swallowed into an empty observation →\n193|    SURVIVED; witness: a torn lease blob turns from `err=… chain is corrupt`\n194|    into `action=parked err=nil`. \"Unknown is never absence\" is pinned only\n195|    for the pane store, not for the lease path.\n196|  - RM2 — materialization arm moved before `authorize` (steps 3/4 swapped) →\n197|    SURVIVED; witness: remote interactive owner + staging journal turns from\n198|    `attach_remote` into `parked(restore_policy)`. The after-restore\n199|    precedence the scenario table claims to pin is unpinned.\n200|  - RM4 — see P1-3.\n201|  - Killed as expected: RM3 park-reason collapse, RM5 `AttestedServer` arm\n202|    narrowing (the producer never mutated the authorizing arm; RM5 is\n203|    killed only because the fixture's generation string matches), RM6 offer\n204|    emission dropped, RM7 successor sequence; control RC SURVIVED.\n205|\n206|## P3\n207|\n208|- **P3-1** Pre-commit crash leaves `binding-*.tmp` staging garbage that no\n209|  retry sweeps (probe C1: `[binding-2863015058.tmp binding.json]`). Documented\n210|  as ignored; a sweep is cheap.\n211|- **P3-2** Hygiene: TRACEABILITY mutant table lists `N-discovery` twice\n212|  (26 rows shown, \"25 of 25\" claimed; the harness has 25); `doc.go:29` names\n213|  `AuthorizeInput` as composed (it is not); `ParkedPayload`/`checkEvidenceIDs`\n214|  duplicate closed-shape predicates `canonicaljson` already enforces at\n215|  `AppendEvent` (harmless pre-checks, but \"nothing re-implemented\" is\n216|  overstated).\n217|- **P3-3** Landed-gate observation (not this leaf's defect, for the\n218|  orchestrator): `fencing.Authorize` checks grant expiry before ownership\n219|  direction, so a remote interactive owner with a lapsed local grant refuses\n220|  `lease_conflict` instead of offering attach/takeover (probe 10); and\n221|  `sessrepo.checkAppend` accepts a stale-lease append while the tail sits on\n222|  that lease (probe 9). Both deserve their own board items.\n223|\n224|## Coverage statement\n225|\n226|Producer claim: 41 of 41 AC rows driven. Names and call sites resolve, but\n227|**six rows are not faithfully driven per the pinned text**: \"Cached evidence\n228|never authorizes\" (field-name census; P1-2), \"Checkpoint admission gates\n229|resume\" (P1-4), \"Bootstrap idempotency\" (no window; P1-3), \"`session.parked`\n230|authored under lease\" (wrong authority; P1-1), \"After-restore sequence 1-5\"\n231|(step 4/5 label, 3/4 order unpinned; P2-4/P2-5), \"Effective profile derived\n232|with source\" (head, not closure; P2-1). Honest ratio: 35 of 41.\n233|\n234|## Instruments (all in the evidence archive)\n235|\n236|`probes/zz_review_probe_test.go` (16 probes), `probes/zz_review_delta_test.go`\n237|(mutant delta witnesses), `review_mutants.py` (8 rows, whole-suite killer,\n238|raw logs in `logs/mutants/`), `delta_under_mutant.py`, `logs/10-11`\n239|(probe runs), `logs/40-41` (shipped harness ×2 with raw per-plant logs),\n240|`logs/30` (race rerun with uptime before/after), `logs/70-71`, `logs/80`.\n241|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` everywhere; 0 `__pycache__` left.\n242|\n243|Verdict recorded by RUN-260917-3934e0; no product edits, commits,\n244|checkpoints or integration were performed; the isolated copies are deleted\n245|after attachment.","final_result":true}}}
